dsh: reasoning:
Now I understand the state. The order W07c-B asks:
1. Blocks per slot: count distinct blocks by hash (each block once, taking its slot from any event that carries it), include all slots in the range [min, max] of observed slots, including those with 0 blocks. Publish distribution (p50, p95, max) and mean `distinct blocks / slots in interval`.
2. Parents per block and fraction of reds: also by distinct block (once per hash); if two nodes report different values for the same block, count and report (would be a finding).
3. Review whether any other §3 metric counts the same block multiple times unintentionally; if so, correct with the same criterion.
4. Tests: synthetic hand-crafted cases with exact answer (three nodes that see the same blocks; empty slots; a block one node doesn't see); existing tests remain green (updating only those that measured the erroneous thing, one at a time and explained).

